SUMMARY:Toronto Fringe Festival:  Tango After Midnight ($19)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nCan you join us at ***FRINGE***--early
  July??\n\nWe'll attend 'just' three performances.\n\n$19 tickets. Details
  below.\n\n### June 30-July 12\, 2026\n\nWelcome to the **38th annual Toro
 nto Fringe Festival**\, Toronto's place for indie theatre and performance.
  With [123 shows](https://fringetoronto.com/fringe/shows) at [27 venues](h
 ttps://fringetoronto.com/accessibility/access-at-venues/venues) across the
  city!\n\nSunday July 5th (2pm-4pm)\n\n***TANGO After Midnight-- (55 minut
 es)***\n\nAs night falls\, a new dance emerges...\n\nPointeTango—winner 
 of the Toronto Fringe Patrons’ Pick and the B Street Collaborative Dance
  Award—ignites the stage with a striking fusion of pointe shoes and stil
 ettos. This electrifying production blends Argentine tango with classical 
 ballet\, interwoven with cinematic projections filmed on location in Bueno
 s Aires.\n\nFast-paced and visually arresting\, the work features innovati
 ve lighting and sound design\, alongside world-class performers and 2025 C
 anadian Tango Champions Erin Scott-Kafadar and Alexander Richardson.\n\n**
 A 15-time Fringe Award–winning company.**\n\n★★★★★ “Breathta
 king artistry” –Winnipeg Free Press\n★★★★★ “They dance as 
 one body\, with grace and precision” –Monday Magazine\n\n**Ticket link
  here**--(our group will attend Sunday July 5th)\n\nhttps://fringetoronto.
 com/fringe/show/tango-after-midnight\n\nDon't delay--Fringe tickets sell o
 ut quickly! $19 per person.
