SUMMARY:Toronto Fringe Festival:  Night Journey ($19)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nCan you join us at ***FRINGE***--early
  July??\n\nWe'll attend 'just' three performances.\n\n$19 tickets. Details
  below.\n\n\\#\\#\\# June 30\\-July 12\\\, 2026\n\nWelcome to the **38th a
 nnual Toronto Fringe Festival**\, Toronto's place for indie theatre and pe
 rformance. With [123 shows](https://fringetoronto.com/fringe/shows) at [27
  venues](https://fringetoronto.com/accessibility/access-at-venues/venues) 
 across the city!\n\nTuesday July 7th (7pm-9pm) ***At the Arts & Letters Cl
 ub!***\n\n**Night Journey-- (80 minutes)**\n\nThis original\, full-length 
 play explores the dynamics among five strangers in a college night class s
 tudying the Greek epic\, The Odyssey. Each is broken in his or her own way
 \; all are in quest of a better life. This challenging work of theatre is 
 brought fully to life by Night Journey's exceptional cast of actors.\n\n**
 Performances are being held at the beautiful Arts and Letters Club of Toro
 nto\, 14 Elm St**. Come early or stay late and enjoy the Club’s lounge o
 r take a tour of our heritage building with its impressive collection of C
 anadian art.\n\n**Ticket link here:** (our group will attend Tuesday July 
 7th)\n\nhttps://fringetoronto.com/fringe/show/night-journey\n\nDon't delay
 --Fringe tickets sell out quickly! $19 per person.\n\nProducer: Martin Jon
 es\, Renée Stein\, Gregory Light\, with the assistance of members of the 
 Arts and Letters Club **and six talented students from Toronto Metropolita
 n University’s School of Performance.**\n\nWe must support this!!
